      "SUZANNE: Not exactly. You collect them.\nSUZANNE: Yes, so?\nGEORGETTE: Gives me an upset stomach. Like you and horsemeat.\nSUZANNE: It's nothing to do with my digestion : it's my memories. I'd rather eat human flesh.",
      "GEORGETTE: Really?\nAMELIE: What did I say?\nSUZANNE: No-one out. who's come in today hasn't said how nice it is •",
      "AMELIE: Camel filters pl. .. oops 1 ',\nAMELIE: Oh God, I'm so sorry'\nGEORGETTE: Oh, well done' Do excuse me, I'll be right back.",
      "GINA: I'm getting to know her a bit. She's not exactly wild, but you do have to tame her.\nTHE CONCIERGE: Ah ... the pretty girl from the fifth floor! I just have to tell you something unbelievable ... do you believe in miracles?\nAMELIE: Not today, no.\nAMELIE: Oh. . . really .. ?"
    ]
